title RecruitBook Batch 2 — Student Profile Foundation — Misuse Cases

left to right direction

' ============================================================
' LAYOUT: adversaries (left) -> misuse cases (center) ->
' grouped security controls (right). One primary control
' group per misuse case keeps the arrow set small.
' ============================================================

rectangle "RecruitBook Student Profile Foundation — Misuse Cases" {

  ' ----------------------- LEFT: adversaries -----------------------
  package "Adversaries" as PKG_Adversaries {
    actor "Malicious Student" as MaliciousStudent
    actor "Unauthorized Counselor" as UnauthCounselor
    actor "Unauthorized\nAdmissions Officer" as UnauthAdmissions
    actor "Unauthenticated\nAttacker" as UnauthAttacker
  }

  ' ----------------------- CENTER: misuse cases --------------------
  ' Labels carry the target, so no separate targets package is needed.
  package "Misuse Cases" as PKG_Misuse {
    usecase "Forge profile_id to read\nanother student's profile" as MUC_ReadOther
    usecase "Forge profile_id to edit\nanother student's profile" as MUC_EditOther
    usecase "Tamper with client-side\nrole / status" as MUC_RoleTamper
    usecase "Counselor / admissions\nearly access attempt" as MUC_EarlyAccess
    usecase "Premature draft\nprofile exposure" as MUC_DraftExposure
    usecase "Oversized narrative input" as MUC_Oversized
    usecase "XSS / script payload\nin narrative" as MUC_XSS
    usecase "Service-role /\nprivileged bypass" as MUC_ServiceRole
  }

  ' ----------------------- RIGHT: control groups -------------------
  package "Security Controls" as PKG_Controls {
    usecase "Route Guard +\nServer Reauthorization" as SC_RouteReauth
    usecase "Owner-Only RLS +\nOwnership Helper" as SC_OwnerRLS
    usecase "No Counselor /\nAdmissions Access" as SC_NoCounselorAdmissions
    usecase "Plain-Text\nNarrative Safety" as SC_PlainText
    usecase "Zero Service-Role\nUsage" as SC_NoServiceRole
    usecase "Platform Admin\nRead-Only Access" as SC_AdminReadOnly
  }

}

' ============================================================
' ADVERSARY -> MISUSE CASE
' ============================================================

MaliciousStudent --> MUC_ReadOther
MaliciousStudent --> MUC_EditOther
MaliciousStudent --> MUC_DraftExposure
MaliciousStudent --> MUC_Oversized
MaliciousStudent --> MUC_XSS

UnauthCounselor --> MUC_EarlyAccess
UnauthAdmissions --> MUC_EarlyAccess

UnauthAttacker --> MUC_RoleTamper
UnauthAttacker --> MUC_ServiceRole

' ============================================================
' MISUSE CASE -> ONE PRIMARY CONTROL GROUP (mitigated by)
' ============================================================

MUC_ReadOther ..> SC_OwnerRLS : mitigated by
MUC_EditOther ..> SC_OwnerRLS : mitigated by
MUC_RoleTamper ..> SC_RouteReauth : mitigated by
MUC_EarlyAccess ..> SC_NoCounselorAdmissions : mitigated by
MUC_DraftExposure ..> SC_AdminReadOnly : mitigated by
MUC_Oversized ..> SC_PlainText : mitigated by
MUC_XSS ..> SC_PlainText : mitigated by
MUC_ServiceRole ..> SC_NoServiceRole : mitigated by

' ============================================================
' NOTES (short)
' ============================================================

note bottom of SC_OwnerRLS
  Form IDs are lookup keys only.
  is_profile_owner(profile_id) resolves
  ownership; a non-owner reads/writes nothing.
end note

note bottom of SC_NoCounselorAdmissions
  No counselor/admissions profile visibility
  in Batch 2 (deny-by-default). Access is added
  deliberately in Batch 3 / Batch 4.
end note

note bottom of SC_PlainText
  Plain text only: server-side length caps and
  JSX escaping. No markdown, no
  dangerouslySetInnerHTML.
end note

note bottom of SC_AdminReadOnly
  platform_admin is SELECT-only via
  is_platform_admin(); no admin write path.
  Completion is derived, not stored.
end note

